======================================================================
  5. Interaction: does the infection response differ by sex?
======================================================================
Genes with a significant sex x time interaction (LRT, FDR 5%): 3 
[1] "Intercept"          "sex_Male_vs_Female" "time_Day4_vs_Day0" 
[4] "time_Day8_vs_Day0"  "sexMale.timeDay4"   "sexMale.timeDay8"  
Interpreting interaction coefficients:
  time_Day8_vs_Day0          = Day8 effect in FEMALES (reference sex)
  sexMale.timeDay8           = how much the Day8 effect DIFFERS in males
  Day8 effect in males       = time_Day8_vs_Day0 + sexMale.timeDay8
  saved: results/07_multifactor/interaction_top_genes.png
With 3-4 mice per sex x time cell, interaction tests have LOW power.
 A non-significant interaction is NOT evidence that males and females respond
 the same. Plan ~2-4x more replicates if interactions are the main question.

Group design: Day8 response in females: 4959 genes, in males: 4028 genes.
 Classic trap: 'genes significant in males but not females' is NOT a test of
 difference. Only the interaction test answers that question.

